        "execSummary":  "The data makes a stark case: without a unified AI platform, governance friction will strangle ROI regardless of how much the organization spends on models and tools. Only 1 in 12 enterprises has solved this, meaning the majority are burning budget on fragmented deployments that cannot pass their own governance gates. For senior leaders, this reframes the AI investment conversation—the ROI constraint is not model capability or data quality, it is platform standardization and governance velocity. Security concerns and data integration challenges are blocking agentic AI returns for roughly 40% and 38% of organizations respectively, making those the near-term priorities.",
