        "summary":  "A Thoughtworks survey of 3,200 global CIOs reveals no dominant governance model for enterprise AI, with oversight distributed across central IT, executive leadership, and dedicated AI roles. Despite high visibility into AI deployments, 94% of U.S. CIOs report being held accountable for security breaches or compliance failures caused by AI systems deployed by other parts of the organization. Eighty-eight percent acknowledge AI adoption is outpacing their governance implementation.",
