        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "AWS released Strands Box, an open-source sandbox tool in developer preview that restricts AI agent actions using behavioral policies written in Dogwood, an AWS-developed policy language, combining OS-level isolation with network gateway controls. The tool allows administrators to enforce behavioral rate limits and access rules externally—without relying on the agent itself to remember constraints—and can attach credentials to approved requests without exposing secrets to the agent. Current limitations include macOS-only support and files accessed via built-in tools remaining outside policy evaluation.",
        "execSummary":  "Strands Box addresses one of the most pressing enterprise blockers for agentic AI: reliably preventing agents from taking unauthorized actions without depending on the model\u0027s own compliance. By moving enforcement to the OS and network layer with an external policy language, AWS gives security teams a control plane they own rather than one baked into model behavior. For enterprise security and risk leaders, the architectural principle here—behavioral containment at the infrastructure layer—is more important than the specific tool, as it will need to extend to non-AWS environments. The current macOS-only constraint and the gap around built-in tool file access are meaningful limitations that must be resolved before this is production-ready in enterprise environments.",
