        "theme":  "Platforms",
        "summary":  "David Linthicum examines why neoclouds—specialized GPU infrastructure providers optimized for AI workloads—are growing at 58% CAGR toward a projected $400 billion market by 2031, yet struggle to gain enterprise adoption despite $25 billion in 2025 revenue. The core problem is a marketing and positioning failure: enterprise architects cannot identify where neoclouds fit in their existing reference architectures. The solution prescribes a mature enterprise sales motion led by solutions architects who can articulate security, governance, and architectural fit—not raw GPU performance.",
