        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "A survey of 300 technology executives found that only about one-third of agentic AI projects advance to production, with data fragmentation and insufficient knowledge frameworks as primary obstacles. Organizations with stronger semantic knowledge capabilities achieve significantly higher production rates (61% vs. 34% average). Companies plan to invest in retrieval technologies, knowledge graphs, and AI evaluation agents to close this gap.",
        "execSummary":  "Most enterprise AI agent projects are stalling before they reach production—the bottleneck is not model capability but organizational knowledge infrastructure. Only 34% of agentic projects make it to production on average, while companies with robust semantic and knowledge-graph foundations hit 61%. For enterprise and customer-support leaders, this means the critical investment is not in adding more agents but in structuring the data and context those agents need to act reliably. The key caveat: this report is produced in partnership with Neo4j, a graph-database vendor, so the emphasis on knowledge graphs reflects a commercial framing.",
